;; Seatbelt jail for the GRADED RE-RUN of the hidden fail-to-pass suite
;; (real_gate.sh run_one, "Graded-by-default" block). The model session itself
;; is already jailed by gate.sb; this profile jails the grading process, which
;; is distinct because it intentionally EXECUTES model-authored src (the grader
;; imports it) OUTSIDE the session. Before 2026-08-20 that re-run was
;; unsandboxed and two forgeries were measured (SECURITY_BOUNDARY.md, reporter
;; path F2/F3): src read the admitted case pin from the `<workdir>.row-context
;; .json` sibling and re-registered trivial passing tests, and detached
;; children rewrote the TAP destination after node exited. This profile denies
;; both.
;;
;; Rules of the jail:
;;  - READ: the workdir (src + restored pristine tests + copied hidden grader),
;;    the gate-owned preload copy, and ordinary runtime reads (node binary,
;;    dyld caches, /usr/lib). Kernel-denied: the case pin, the private evidence
;;    directory holding the TAP, the harness repo, and the public mirror. src
;;    runs, but it cannot learn the admitted case names from the pin, read the
;;    evidence back, or reach graders/manifests of other fixtures.
;;  - EVIDENCE CHANNEL: the TAP destination is HIDDEN, not merely fenced. The
;;    gate opens the evidence file itself and passes `/dev/fd/N` to the node
;;    test runner; node --test executes each test file in a CHILD process that
;;    does not inherit that fd, so model code gets ENXIO on the fd and EPERM on
;;    the path (both measured 2026-08-20) — there is no addressable evidence
;;    location inside the jail at all. Writes are fenced to /dev/fd (the
;;    runner's channel), a gate-owned scratch dir, and the null devices.
;;    Everything else — including the workdir itself — is write-denied: the
;;    re-run scores the state the model left, it never mutates it.
;;  - NETWORK: denied outright; grading needs no egress.
;;
;; Ordering is load-bearing and was measured on this host: specific denies must
;; stand BEFORE `(allow default)` to win, and every path must be the REAL path
;; (macOS resolves /tmp -> /private/tmp before Seatbelt matching). real_gate.sh
;; renders the absolute paths below per run (Seatbelt has no env vars) and
;; REFUSES graded scoring when sandbox-exec is unavailable — a hidden grader is
;; never re-run unsandboxed (fail-closed).
(version 1)
;; The admitted case pin: knowledge of the expected case names is what let a
;; forged suite re-register them as trivial passes (F2). Deny-by-literal first.
(deny file-read* (literal "__PIN__"))
;; The private grade evidence directory (TAP + seals): invisible and untouched
;; from inside the jail. The only channel out is the gate-opened /dev/fd below.
(deny file-read* (subpath "__EVIDENCE__"))
;; The evaluation harness and its public mirror (hidden graders of OTHER
;; fixtures, Git objects, the approved manifests that carry the pins) stay
;; denied. The runner-owned assertion-freeze preload (F1 mitigation) is COPIED
;; by real_gate.sh into __GRADE_TMP__ before the re-run and imported from
;; there: an allow-literal under a denied subpath does NOT work — the ESM
;; resolver realpaths the parent directory and trips the directory deny
;; (measured 2026-08-20). The copy is gate-owned; reads follow (allow default).
(deny file-read* (subpath "__HARNESS__"))
(deny file-read* (subpath "__MIRROR__"))
(allow default)
(deny network*)
(deny file-write*)
(allow file-write*
  (subpath "/dev/fd")
  (subpath "__GRADE_TMP__")
  (literal "/dev/null")
  (literal "/dev/dtracehelper"))
